From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 11:13:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Docs/admin-guide/mm/damon/usage: update for hugepage_size

Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 Documentation/admin-guide/mm/damon/usage.rst | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/damon/usage.rst b/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/damon/usage.rst
index 56e0c4d972ac5..18b96c667bd98 100644
--- a/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/damon/usage.rst
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/mm/damon/usage.rst
@@ -78,7 +78,7 @@ comma (",").
     │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ 0/prep_action
     │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ ...
     │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ filters/nr_filters
-    │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ 0/type,matching,allow,path
+    │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ 0/type,matching,allow,path,min,max
     │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ │ ...
     │ │ │ │ │ │ │ ...
     │ │ │ │ │ :ref:`targets <sysfs_targets>`/nr_targets
@@ -309,6 +309,8 @@ Writing a number (``N``) to the file creates the number of child directories
 named ``0`` to ``N-1``.  Each directory represents each filter and works in a
 way similar to that for :ref:`DAMOS filter <sysfs_filters>`.  When the filter
 ``type`` is ``memcg``, ``path`` file acts as ``memcg_path`` for :ref:`DAMOS
+filter <sysfs_filters>`.  When the filter ``type`` is ``hugepage_size``,
+``min`` and ``max`` files acts as files of the same names for :ref:`DAMOS
 filter <sysfs_filters>`.
 
 .. _sysfs_targets:
